---
import Section from "../site/Section.astro"
import Split from "../site/Split.astro"
import Stage from "../site/Stage.astro"
import NewObservation from "../product/NewObservation.astro"
---

<Section ruled={false}>
  <Split>
    <div slot="start" class="copy">
      <h2 class="h2">Start with a title, or with a question.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        New observation takes a title and a folder, and Create opens the page. In the terminal,
        <span class="mono">observe o new</span> takes the same and, with <span class="mono">--text</span> or
        <span class="mono">--text-file</span>, adds your first note as a text block.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        Or ask the agent a question. Every investigation opens an observation, shows its run on the page while it works, and writes its
        conclusion and evidence there as blocks. That needs a model on the server.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div slot="end" data-in-view="rise">
      <Stage><NewObservation /></Stage>
    </div>
  </Split>
</Section>

<style>
  .copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .copy .lead {
    font-size: 17px;
  }
</style>
